{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The last bucket was overflowing. `bucket_of` used `value // width` with no upper bound, so a value sitting on the top edge (`value == width * n_buckets`) came back as index `n_buckets` instead of `n_buckets - 1`.\n\nWith width 10 and 3 buckets, 30 landed in index 3. That index does not exist, so the bar was wrong and `histogram_summary` raised an `IndexError` when it tried to increment that count.\n\nThe index is now clamped to the last bucket. 30 maps to 2, and the summary for `[0, 10, 20, 30]` is `{n: 4, counts: [1, 1, 2]}`. Interior values are unchanged."}]},"session_id":"140fac37-92d0-42a9-b712-478123eb237c"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":83211,"duration_api_ms":83211,"is_error":false,"result":"I'll look through the histogram chart code and how the last bucket is computed so we can see why the bars are off and why that bucket errors.The last bucket overflows: a value on the top edge is indexed past the end, which both mis-counts that bar and raises an error. I'll clamp that edge into the final bucket.The last bucket was overflowing. `bucket_of` used `value // width` with no upper bound, so a value sitting on the top edge (`value == width * n_buckets`) came back as index `n_buckets` instead of `n_buckets - 1`.\n\nWith width 10 and 3 buckets, 30 landed in index 3. That index does not exist, so the bar was wrong and `histogram_summary` raised an `IndexError` when it tried to increment that count.\n\nThe index is now clamped to the last bucket. 30 maps to 2, and the summary for `[0, 10, 20, 30]` is `{n: 4, counts: [1, 1, 2]}`. Interior values are unchanged.","session_id":"140fac37-92d0-42a9-b712-478123eb237c","request_id":"6c56b45f-228f-4c03-9bc5-32e686856e05","usage":{"inputTokens":16402,"outputTokens":3673,"cacheReadTokens":81792,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
